IMPORT prelude

-- Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (Western Australia) -- the home owner contracting a builder: is my contract covered,
-- what must it contain, how much may the builder take up front, how may it be varied or the price raised, must the work be
-- insured, and what can I do, and by when, if it goes wrong.
--
-- SEAT: the home owner contracting a builder -- the "owner", "the person for whom ... home building work is to be performed
-- under the contract" (s 3(1)). Every exported question is phrased as that owner would ask it. Where the Act addresses only
-- the builder (ss 4(4), 5(2), 7(3), 10, 13, 25C) or the insurer (s 25D), what is encoded is what the owner must be given, what
-- may be asked of the owner, and what the owner may do about it.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3(1) ("home building work", "home building work contract", "cost plus contract", "associated work");
-- s 4 (writing, signature, the prescribed notice, termination under s 4(5)); s 5 (copy of the contract); ss 7 and 8
-- (variations, and the two exceptions with the 10-working-day statement and the 10-working-day complaint window); s 9 with
-- Schedule 1 cll 1-3 (the 45-working-day building permit condition and what follows if it fails); s 10 (deposit and
-- progress payments, termination under s 10(4)); s 11 (defects notified within 4 months of practical completion); s 13 (the
-- rise-and-fall prohibition and the s 13(4) exceptions) with Schedule 1 cl 4 (termination for a price rise over 5%); s 14
-- (cost plus contracts); s 19 (how the owner terminates); s 26(2) (restrictions on inspection); s 28 (no contracting out);
-- Part 3A ss 25A, 25B, 25C(1), (2), 25D(1)(a), (d), (e) (home indemnity insurance for work done by a builder).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (Act No. 61 of 1991) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_45904.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 45904, retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit states
-- no compilation number or date; its compilation table ends with the Directors' Liability Reform Act 2023 Pt. 3 Div. 34
-- (in operation 5 Apr 2023). Regulations: Home Building Contracts Regulations 1992, version 03-k0-00, currency from
-- 1 Sep 2025, as deposited at ../../../home-building-contracts-regulations-1992/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48796.txt
-- (mrdoc 48796, retrieved 2026-10-20): r 2A ($7 500 and $500 000 for the s 3 definition), r 3 with Schedule 1 (the notice
-- for the home owner), r 3A (20% deposit for cabinetry work), r 5 ($500 maximum excess), r 7 ($20 000 minimum amount for
-- s 25A), r 7A ($40 000 deposit cover), r 7B ($200 000 minimum cover).
--
-- Working days (s 3(1): "Monday to Friday but excluding ... a day that is a public holiday") and months are entered as
-- counts the owner states; this encoding does no calendar arithmetic.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: unconscionable, harsh or oppressive conduct (s 15) and misleading or deceptive conduct (s 15A), which are
-- judgments for the Building Commissioner or the State Administrative Tribunal on a complaint; understated prime cost items
-- (s 12, a builder's offence turning on what the item "could reasonably cost"); transportable and prefabricated dwellings
-- (ss 10(2), 25D(2), (3)); Schedule 1 cl 5 (review of a price rise) beyond the owner's right to complain; the adjustment of
-- rights after termination (s 20) beyond the right to complain; owner-builders (Part 3A Division 3) and the builder's own
-- home exemption (s 25B(3), (4)); approved funds (Division 3A) except as an alternative to a policy; the notices required
-- in or after a Minister's exemption period (ss 25I-25L), where being in such a period is one FACT; the builder's fines,
-- prosecutions and infringement notices (ss 30-31B, r 8); review, regulations and retrospectivity (ss 25H, 32-34). The
-- complaint itself is made under the Building Services (Complaint Resolution and Administration) Act 2011, which is not
-- encoded; its time limits are read only from the prescribed notice in Schedule 1 to the Regulations.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the home owner, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Home Building Contracts Act 1991 -- the home owner contracting a builder`

§§ `s 3 -- the work and the contract`

-- s 3(1): "home building work means the whole or part of the work of -- (a) constructing or reconstructing a dwelling ...;
-- or (b) placing a dwelling on land; or (c) altering, improving or repairing a dwelling ...; or (d) constructing or carrying
-- out any associated work". "associated work includes site works, swimming pools, spas, pergolas, carports, garages, sheds,
-- fencing, retaining walls, paving, driveways, landscaping and other like works". Which the work is, is a FACT the owner
-- states. Part 3A (s 25A "residential building work") treats associated work differently according to whether the same
-- contract also includes (a), (b) or (c) work, so that is split here.
DECLARE `Kind of work` IS ONE OF
    `building or rebuilding a home`
    `placing a home on land`
    `altering, improving or repairing a home`
    `associated work with building, placing or altering a home in the same contract`
    `associated work only`

-- One case is one contract between the owner and a builder (s 3(1) "contract means a home building work contract").
DECLARE Contract HAS
    `kind of work` IS A `Kind of work`
    -- s 3(1) "cost plus contract": the builder recovers an amount "not determined at the time when the contract is entered
    -- into", being actual cost plus a percentage or a specified sum. A FACT.
    `is a cost plus contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1) para (b)(i): work "for a builder who is in turn obliged to perform the work under another contract".
    `is for a builder who must do the work under another contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1) para (b)(ii), (iii): "the amount stated in the contract as being payable under the contract for the work".
    `amount stated as payable` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 25A "cost of the building work" (b): for a cost plus contract, "the estimated cost of construction specified in the
    -- application for a building permit". 0 if not applicable.
    `estimated cost in the building permit application` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 4(1)
    `is in writing setting out all its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows the date of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is signed by the builder and by me` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(3)
    `I was given the notice before I signed` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10(1)
    `deposit the contract lets the builder take` IS A NUMBER
    `lets the builder take other payments before work starts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lets the builder take payments after work starts that are not for work done or materials supplied` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Regulations r 3A(1), (2): "cabinetry work", and "the value of the off-site work ... is more than 50%".
    `is for cabinetry work, more than half of it off-site` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 14(1)
    `is headed and acknowledged as a cost plus contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25A "developer": "a person for whom residential building work is performed under a building contract in relation
    -- to 4 or more dwellings".
    `number of homes in the contract` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 25B(4A): "(a) a building permit ... is not required for the work; or (b) ... the work is not, or is not part of, a
    -- prescribed building service under the Building Services (Registration) Act 2011". Borrowed terms, asked as FACTS.
    `needs a building permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a prescribed building service` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25C(3) and s 25I: a period of up to 6 months the Minister specifies by order. A FACT.
    `falls in a Minister's insurance exemption period` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3(1): "home building work contract means a contract between a builder and an owner for the performance by the builder
-- of home building work, but does not include -- (a) a cost plus contract; (b) a contract for the performance of home
-- building work -- (i) for a builder who is in turn obliged to perform the work under another contract; or (ii) if the
-- amount stated ... is $6 000, or such other amount as is prescribed, or less; or (iii) if the amount stated ... is
-- $200 000, or such other amount as is prescribed, or more".
-- Regulations r 2A: "(a) the prescribed amount for paragraph (b)(ii) ... is $7 500; and (b) the prescribed amount for
-- paragraph (b)(iii) ... is $500 000."
@export Is my contract one the Home Building Contracts Act covers -- a home building work contract (s 3, r 2A)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract a home building work contract` IF
        (NOT `the contract`'s `is a cost plus contract`)
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `is for a builder who must do the work under another contract`)
    AND `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` GREATER THAN 7500
    AND `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` LESS THAN 500000

§§ `s 4 -- in writing, signed, and the notice`

-- s 4(1): "A contract -- (a) must be in writing -- (i) setting out all of the terms, conditions and provisions of the
-- contract; and (ii) showing the date of the contract; and (b) must be signed by the builder and the owner or their
-- respective agents."
@export Is my contract made the way the Act requires -- in writing, dated, and signed by both of us (s 4(1))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract made as the Act requires` IF
        `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`
    AND `the contract`'s `is in writing setting out all its terms`
    AND `the contract`'s `shows the date of the contract`
    AND `the contract`'s `is signed by the builder and by me`

-- s 4(3): "The owner must be given a notice referred to in subsection (2) before the owner signs a contract." Regulations
-- r 3: "The form of notice set out in Schedule 1 is prescribed" ("NOTICE FOR THE HOME OWNER").
@export Must I be given the Notice for the Home Owner before I sign (s 4(3), r 3)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given the notice before I sign` IF `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`

-- s 5(3): if the owner was not given a copy of the signed contract and "the owner in writing requests the builder to give
-- to the owner a copy of the contract, the builder must comply with that request within 10 working days of receiving it."
@export Within how many working days of my written request must the builder give me a copy of the contract (s 5(3))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy` MEANS
    IF `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract` THEN 10 ELSE 0

§§ `s 10 -- deposit and progress payments`

-- s 10(1): the contract must not entitle the builder to any payment "(a) before the commencement of the home building
-- work ... unless the payment is -- (i) a deposit of not more than 6.5% of the total amount payable to the builder under
-- the contract for the home building work; or (ii) of a prescribed kind". Regulations r 3A(3): for cabinetry work more than
-- half off-site, "the builder may, before the commencement of the home building work, demand payment of a deposit of not
-- more than 20% of the total amount payable".
@export What is the most deposit my builder may take before work starts (s 10(1)(a), r 3A)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most deposit my builder may take` MEANS
    IF `the contract`'s `is for cabinetry work, more than half of it off-site`
    THEN `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` TIMES 65 DIVIDED BY 1000

-- s 10(1): "A builder must not enter into a contract which provides that the builder is entitled to demand or receive from
-- the owner any payment -- (a) before the commencement ... unless ... a deposit [within the cap] ...; (b) after the
-- commencement ... unless the payment is -- (i) a genuine progress payment for work already performed or materials or
-- services already supplied; or (ii) is of a prescribed kind." No payment of a prescribed kind is prescribed in the
-- deposited Regulations other than the r 3A deposit.
@export Do my contract's payment terms break the Act's limits on deposits and progress payments (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my contract's payment terms break the limits` IF
        `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`
    AND (    `the contract`'s `deposit the contract lets the builder take` GREATER THAN `What is the most deposit my builder may take` `the contract`
         OR  `the contract`'s `lets the builder take other payments before work starts`
         OR  `the contract`'s `lets the builder take payments after work starts that are not for work done or materials supplied`)

-- s 10(5): "A builder under a contract must not demand or receive from the owner any payment after the commencement of
-- the home building work unless the payment is a genuine progress payment". s 10(3): a payment demanded "in accordance with"
-- a schedule of stage payments in the contract "is to be taken to be a genuine progress payment ... until the contrary is
-- shown". Whether the contrary has been shown is a judgment on a complaint, asked as a FACT.
@export Once work has started, may my builder demand this payment from me (s 10(3), (5))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `it is for work already done or materials already supplied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment for work already done, or materials or services already supplied?
      `it follows the contract's schedule of stage payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment demanded in accordance with a schedule of stage payments in the contract?
      `it has been shown not to be for work done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been shown (for example on a complaint) that the payment is not for work done or materials supplied?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my builder demand this progress payment` IF
        (NOT `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`)
    OR  `it is for work already done or materials already supplied`
    OR  (`it follows the contract's schedule of stage payments` AND (NOT `it has been shown not to be for work done`))

§§ `ss 4(5), 10(4), 14(3), 19 -- ending the contract for the way it was made`

-- s 14(1): a builder must not enter into a cost plus contract unless it is written and "(a) has a heading at the beginning
-- that includes the words "cost plus contract"; and (b) contains an acknowledgment by the parties that the contract is a
-- cost plus contract and that this Act, apart from this section and Part 3A, does not apply". s 14(2): "Subsection (1) does
-- not apply to a cost plus contract that comes within paragraph (b) of the definition of home building work contract" --
-- so not to a sub-contract, nor where the stated amount is $7 500 or less or $500 000 or more.
@export Is my cost plus contract missing the heading and acknowledgment the Act requires (s 14(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my cost plus contract missing its heading or acknowledgment` IF
        `the contract`'s `is a cost plus contract`
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `is headed and acknowledged as a cost plus contract`)
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `is for a builder who must do the work under another contract`)
    AND `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` GREATER THAN 7500
    AND `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` LESS THAN 500000

-- s 4(5): "If any requirement of subsection (1) is not complied with by the builder the contract may be terminated by the
-- owner in accordance with section 19." s 10(4): "If a builder enters into a contract in breach of subsection (1), the
-- contract may be terminated by the owner". s 14(3): the same for a cost plus contract in breach of s 14(1).
-- s 19(2): the notice "must be in writing signed by the party and must be given to the other party before the completion of
-- the home building work". Note that s 4(5) reaches only s 4(1); not being given the notice (s 4(3)) is not a ground.
@export May I end my contract because of the way it was made, by a signed written notice to the builder (ss 4(5), 10(4), 14(3), 19)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `the work is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the home building work under the contract been completed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` IF
        (NOT `the work is complete`)
    AND (    (`Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract` AND (NOT `Is my contract made as the Act requires` `the contract`))
         OR  `Do my contract's payment terms break the limits` `the contract`
         OR  `Is my cost plus contract missing its heading or acknowledgment` `the contract`)

§§ `ss 7 and 8 -- variations`

-- s 8(1): s 7(1) and (2) do not apply to a variation "made necessary by -- (a) any written direction lawfully given by a
-- person acting under a written law; or (b) circumstances that could not reasonably have been foreseen by the builder at the
-- time when the contract was entered into", if the builder gives the statement in time. s 8(4): (1)(b) does not apply "by
-- reason only of an increase in the costs of labour ... or materials".
DECLARE `Cause of the variation` IS ONE OF
    `a change we agreed`
    `a written direction under a written law`
    `circumstances the builder could not reasonably have foreseen`
    `a rise in the builder's labour or material costs`

-- s 8(1), (2): the builder must give the owner "a statement setting out the reason for, and the cost to be incurred on
-- account of, the variation" (with a copy of any direction) "within 10 working days after the builder -- (a) received
-- notice of the direction ...; or (b) became aware, or should reasonably have become aware, of the circumstances".
-- `working days until the builder's statement` is counted from that point; -1 if no statement was given.
@export Must this variation be put in writing, with its cost, dated and signed by me before it binds me (ss 7(1), 8)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation` @desc What made the variation necessary
      `working days until the builder's statement` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days after the builder got the direction or learned of the circumstances that the builder gave you a written statement of reason and cost; -1 if none
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the variation be in writing and signed by me` IF
        `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`
    AND CONSIDER `the cause`
        WHEN `a change we agreed` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a rise in the builder's labour or material costs` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a written direction under a written law` THEN
            NOT (`working days until the builder's statement` AT LEAST 0 AND `working days until the builder's statement` AT MOST 10)
        WHEN `circumstances the builder could not reasonably have foreseen` THEN
            NOT (`working days until the builder's statement` AT LEAST 0 AND `working days until the builder's statement` AT MOST 10)

-- s 7(1): "A variation of a contract -- (a) must be in writing -- (i) setting out all of the terms of, and the cost of, the
-- variation; (ii) showing the date of the variation; and (b) must be signed by the builder and the owner". s 7(2): the owner
-- "must be given a copy of the signed variation -- (a) as soon as is reasonably practicable ...; and (b) before the work to
-- which the variation relates is commenced."
@export Was my variation made as the Act requires -- written with its terms and cost, dated, signed by both of us, and a copy given to me before the work on it began (s 7(1), (2))?
GIVEN `in writing with its terms and cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the variation in writing, setting out all its terms and its cost?
      `dated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it show the date of the variation?
      `signed by both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it signed by the builder and by you (or your agents)?
      `copy given before the varied work began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a copy of the signed variation before the work it covers began?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my variation made as the Act requires` IF
    `in writing with its terms and cost` AND `dated` AND `signed by both of us` AND `copy given before the varied work began`

-- s 8(3): where the builder gives a statement for unforeseen circumstances and "the owner considers that the variation is
-- not one to which subsection (1) applies, the owner cannot make a complaint as provided in section 17 unless the owner makes
-- the complaint within 10 working days after the statement was given to the owner."
@export If I think the builder's "unforeseen circumstances" are not unforeseen, within how many working days of the statement must I complain (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation` @desc What the builder says made the variation necessary
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Within how many working days must I dispute an unforeseen variation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `circumstances the builder could not reasonably have foreseen` THEN 10
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 13 and Schedule 1 cl 4 -- the fixed price and price rises`

-- s 13(1), (2): "A builder must not enter into a contract that contains a rise-and-fall clause"; such a clause "is void".
-- (3): a rise-and-fall clause lets the price "change to reflect changes in the costs of labour ... or materials". (4): a
-- clause is not one "by reason only that it allows a builder to increase the stipulated price to reflect further costs
-- actually imposed on or incurred by the builder -- (a) as a direct consequence of a written law ...; or (b) on account of
-- an increase in any tax, duty or other charge ... after the date of the contract; or (c) by reason of a delay in the
-- commencement ... beyond 45 working days after the date of the contract being a delay -- (i) that is caused solely by the
-- failure of the owner to comply with a condition ...; or (ii) that occurs without any failure on the part of either".
DECLARE `Reason for a price rise` IS ONE OF
    `a rise in labour or material costs`
    `a cost imposed directly by a written law`
    `a rise in a tax, duty or charge after the contract date`
    `a start delayed over 45 working days by my failure alone`
    `a start delayed over 45 working days with neither of us at fault`
    `a start delayed over 45 working days by the builder`

@export Can my builder put my price up for this reason (s 13)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `the reason` IS A `Reason for a price rise` @desc Why the builder wants to raise the price
      `my contract has a clause allowing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract contain a clause allowing a rise for that reason?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my builder raise my price` IF
        `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`
    AND `my contract has a clause allowing it`
    AND CONSIDER `the reason`
        WHEN `a rise in labour or material costs` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a start delayed over 45 working days by the builder` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Schedule 1 cl 4: where cl 2 or 3 or s 13(4)(c) applies, "(b) if the amount of an increase exceeds 5% of the price
-- stipulated in the contract, the owner may terminate the contract in accordance with section 19 within 10 working days
-- after receipt of notice under paragraph (a); and (c) if the owner so terminates the contract, the owner is liable to
-- compensate the builder for the reasonable costs incurred by the builder up to the date of termination."
@export After a notified price rise for a delayed start or a late permit, may I end the contract (Schedule 1 cl 4(b))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the price increase in the builder's notice
      `working days since I received the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since you received the builder's written notice of the increase
      `the work is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the home building work been completed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I terminate because of the price rise` IF
        `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`
    AND `the increase` GREATER THAN `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100
    AND `working days since I received the notice` AT MOST 10
    AND (NOT `the work is complete`)

@export If I end the contract over a price rise, must I pay the builder's reasonable costs up to then (Schedule 1 cl 4(c))?
GIVEN `I terminated under clause 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you terminate under Schedule 1 clause 4(b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay the builder's reasonable costs` IF `I terminated under clause 4`

§§ `s 9 and Schedule 1 cll 1-3 -- the building permit condition`

-- s 9(1): "every contract is conditional upon -- (a) a building permit being granted ... within 45 working days from the
-- date of the contract" (and Water Services Act clearance in the same period). s 9(5)(b): the condition does not apply
-- "where the only work to be performed under the contract is the construction or carrying out of associated work".
-- Schedule 1: cl 1 (builder solely at fault): "the contract is not affected but remains in force on the same terms and
-- conditions except as otherwise agreed"; cll 2 and 3 (owner solely at fault; both or neither): the contract "remains in
-- force ... until the parties agree otherwise, but subject to the provisions of clause 4" (the builder may raise the price).
-- Who was at fault (who failed their s 9(2) obligations) is a FACT.
DECLARE `Who failed` IS ONE OF
    `the builder alone`
    `me alone`
    `both of us`
    `neither of us`

DECLARE `Permit outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the permit condition does not apply`
    `the contract stays in force on the same terms`
    `the contract stays in force but the builder may raise the price by notice`

@export If the building permit is not granted within 45 working days, what happens to my contract (s 9, Schedule 1 cll 1-3)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `who failed` IS A `Who failed` @desc Whose failure to do what s 9(2) required meant the permit was not granted in time
GIVETH A `Permit outcome`
`What happens if the permit is late` MEANS
    IF (NOT `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`)
    THEN `the permit condition does not apply`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the contract`'s `kind of work`
         WHEN `associated work only` THEN `the permit condition does not apply`
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `who failed`
             WHEN `the builder alone` THEN `the contract stays in force on the same terms`
             OTHERWISE `the contract stays in force but the builder may raise the price by notice`

§§ `s 11 -- defects`

-- s 11(1): "the builder is liable to make good at the cost of the builder defects in the home building work notified in
-- writing to the builder within the period of 4 months commencing on the day of practical completion." (1a): a contract may
-- give "a period greater than 4 months". (2): "defect" excludes "a failure for which the builder is specifically declared by
-- the contract to be not liable". Whether something is a defect (workmanship, merchantable quality) is a FACT.
@export Must my builder make good this defect at the builder's own cost (s 11)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `months after practical completion I notified it in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months after practical completion you notified the defect in writing (0 = within the first month); -1 if not notified in writing
      `longer period in my contract in months` IS A NUMBER @desc A notification period longer than 4 months given by your contract, in months; 0 if none
      `the contract declares the builder not liable for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract specifically declare the builder not liable for this failure?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my builder make good this defect` IF
        `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`
    AND (NOT `the contract declares the builder not liable for it`)
    AND `months after practical completion I notified it in writing` AT LEAST 0
    AND (    `months after practical completion I notified it in writing` LESS THAN 4
         OR  `months after practical completion I notified it in writing` LESS THAN `longer period in my contract in months`)

§§ `ss 26 and 28 -- inspection and no contracting out`

-- s 26(2): "A provision in a contract that prohibits or restricts inspection of home building work is void except to the
-- extent that it -- (a) restricts inspection to the builder's normal working hours; or (b) precludes inspection that would
-- unreasonably impede or interfere with the building work."
DECLARE `Inspection restriction` IS ONE OF
    `no inspection at all`
    `only with the builder's consent`
    `only in the builder's normal working hours`
    `none that would unreasonably impede the work`

@export Is this restriction on my inspecting the work binding on me (s 26(2))?
GIVEN `the restriction` IS AN `Inspection restriction` @desc What your contract says about inspecting the work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this inspection restriction binding` IF
    CONSIDER `the restriction`
    WHEN `only in the builder's normal working hours` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `none that would unreasonably impede the work` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 28(1): "An agreement or arrangement that purports to exclude or restrict the operation of any provision of this Act or
-- to modify any such provision to the disadvantage of an owner is to that extent void." (2): "A purported waiver of a right
-- conferred by or under this Act is void."
@export Does a term by which I give up a right the Act gives me bind me (s 28)?
GIVEN `it is to my disadvantage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term exclude, restrict or modify the Act to your disadvantage, or waive a right it gives you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my waiver bind me` IF NOT `it is to my disadvantage`

§§ `Part 3A -- home indemnity insurance`

-- s 25A "cost of the building work": "(a) ... under a residential building work contract, the amount payable under the
-- contract; or (b) ... [otherwise] the estimated cost of construction specified in the application for a building permit".
-- A cost plus contract is not a "residential building work contract" (s 25A), so (b) applies to it.
@export What is the "cost of the building work" for home indemnity insurance (s 25A)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the cost of my building work` MEANS
    IF `the contract`'s `is a cost plus contract`
    THEN `the contract`'s `estimated cost in the building permit application`
    ELSE `the contract`'s `amount stated as payable`

-- s 25A "residential building work means home building work that is -- (a) ... paragraph (a), (b) or (c) ...; or (b) ...
-- paragraph (d) ... when -- (i) it is to be performed under a contract which also includes ... (a), (b) or (c) ...; or (ii)
-- it is associated work of a prescribed kind, but does not include home building work where the cost of the building work
-- is the minimum amount or less". "minimum amount means $10 000 or such other amount as is prescribed"; Regulations r 7:
-- "the minimum amount is prescribed to be $20 000". No associated work is prescribed under (b)(ii) in the deposited
-- Regulations.
@export Is my work "residential building work" for home indemnity insurance (s 25A, r 7)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work residential building work` IF
        `What is the cost of my building work` `the contract` GREATER THAN 20000
    AND CONSIDER `the contract`'s `kind of work`
        WHEN `associated work only` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 25B(1): Division 2 "applies to residential building work that is, or is to be, performed by a builder on behalf of
-- another person". (4A): not if no building permit is required, or the work is not a prescribed building service.
-- s 25C(1): "A builder must not perform residential building work to which this Division applies unless -- (a) a policy of
-- insurance that complies with this Division is in force ...; or (b) corresponding cover is provided by an approved fund".
-- (3): not during, or under a permit granted during, a period specified by order under s 25I. The sub-contract exclusion is
-- in the s 25A definitions of "building contract" and "residential building work contract".
@export Must my builder have home indemnity insurance (or approved-fund cover) for my work (ss 25B, 25C(1))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my builder insure my work` IF
        `Is my work residential building work` `the contract`
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `is for a builder who must do the work under another contract`)
    AND `the contract`'s `needs a building permit`
    AND `the contract`'s `is a prescribed building service`
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `falls in a Minister's insurance exemption period`)

-- s 25C(2): the builder must not perform the work "under a residential building work contract unless the owner has been
-- furnished, prior to a demand from the builder for any payment in relation to the residential building work including any
-- deposit ..., with a certificate in a form approved by the Minister" evidencing the policy or cover.
@export Must I be given the insurance certificate before the builder asks me for any payment, even the deposit (s 25C(2))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I get the insurance certificate before any payment` IF
        `Must my builder insure my work` `the contract`
    AND (NOT `the contract`'s `is a cost plus contract`)

@export May my builder ask me for this deposit now (ss 10(1)(a), 25C(2))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `the deposit asked` IS A NUMBER @desc The deposit the builder is asking for before work starts
      `I have the insurance certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given the certificate of home indemnity insurance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my builder ask me for this deposit` IF
        (    (NOT `Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`)
         OR  `the deposit asked` AT MOST `What is the most deposit my builder may take` `the contract`)
    AND (`I have the insurance certificate` OR (NOT `Must I get the insurance certificate before any payment` `the contract`))

-- s 25D(1)(e): the policy must provide "insurance cover of -- (i) at least $100 000 or such other amount as is prescribed;
-- or (ii) the cost of the building work, whichever is the lesser". Regulations r 7B: "an amount of $200 000 is prescribed".
@export At least how much must the home indemnity insurance cover me for (s 25D(1)(e), r 7B)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must the insurance cover me for` MEANS
    IF (NOT `Must my builder insure my work` `the contract`) THEN 0
    ELSE IF `What is the cost of my building work` `the contract` LESS THAN 200000
         THEN `What is the cost of my building work` `the contract`
         ELSE 200000

-- s 25D(1)(a): for work "under a residential building work contract" for a person "other than a developer", the policy
-- insures "(i) loss of an amount paid by way of deposit ..., up to a limit of $20 000 or another prescribed limit" because a
-- relevant circumstance exists (the builder has died, cannot be found, ceased to exist, is insolvent, or lost registration on
-- financial grounds: s 25D(1A)). Regulations r 7A: "the prescribed limit is $40 000". s 25A: a developer has 4 or more
-- dwellings built under the contract.
@export How much of my deposit is insured if my builder dies, disappears, becomes insolvent or loses registration (s 25D(1)(a)(i), r 7A)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
      `deposit I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The deposit you paid
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my deposit is insured` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `Must my builder insure my work` `the contract`)
        OR `the contract`'s `is a cost plus contract`
        OR `the contract`'s `number of homes in the contract` AT LEAST 4
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `deposit I paid` LESS THAN 40000 THEN `deposit I paid` ELSE 40000

-- s 25D(1)(d): the policy must provide "that claims may be made under it at any time before the expiration of a period of
-- 6 years from the day of practical completion".
@export For how many years after practical completion can I claim on the home indemnity insurance (s 25D(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`For how many years can I claim on the insurance` MEANS
    IF `Must my builder insure my work` `the contract` THEN 6 ELSE 0

-- Regulations r 5: "A policy of insurance under Part 3A of the Act may provide for an amount of $500 or a lesser amount for
-- which the insurer is not liable on a claim under the policy."
@export What is the most excess the home indemnity policy may make me bear on a claim (r 5)?
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract @desc Your contract with the builder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most excess on my claim` MEANS
    IF `Must my builder insure my work` `the contract` THEN 500 ELSE 0

§§ `Disputes -- the time limits in the Notice for the Home Owner`

-- s 17: the owner "may make a complaint under section 5(2) of" the Building Services (Complaint Resolution and
-- Administration) Act 2011 for a breach of the contract or of Part 2. That Act is not encoded. Its time limits are taken
-- from the prescribed notice (Regulations Schedule 1, "Disputes"): a contract complaint "must be made within 3 years from
-- when you became entitled to take legal action"; a complaint about the standard of building services "must be made within
-- 6 years from the time the building service is completed".
DECLARE `Kind of complaint` IS ONE OF
    `a breach of the contract or of Part 2`
    `building work not done in a proper and proficient manner`

@export Within how many years must I complain to the Building Commissioner (s 17; Notice for the Home Owner, "Disputes")?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of complaint` @desc What the complaint is about
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Within how many years must I complain` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a breach of the contract or of Part 2` THEN 3
    WHEN `building work not done in a proper and proficient manner` THEN 6
